# Windows is the primary development platform here, and core.autocrlf=true is the
# common local setting. Without this file, `npm run build:ext` writes LF, git wants
# CRLF in the working tree, and `git status` reports extension/vendor/ as modified
# when the content is byte-identical -- which is noise sitting directly on top of the
# "extension/vendor/ is not stale" CI invariant.
#
# Normalise to LF in the repository for everything textual. CI runs the sync check on
# Linux, so the committed form has to be the Linux form.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Generated by scripts/build-extension.js. Marked so a reviewer sees the diff collapsed
# and does not spend time reading a copy of a file they already reviewed at the source.
extension/vendor/*.js linguist-generated=true

# Binary. Never touch the bytes, never try to diff them as text.
*.png binary
